11.0.0 — Bar LFO, lights left dark when the app lets go, MTC chase over a looping song

What is new since 10051. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds and tests; nothing
here is device-verified yet.
- Modulate (a track's or the master's menu): a new source "Bar LFO", a sine over each bar read
  from the song position. It moves volume, pan, sends and instrument values, and an export moves
  exactly as playback does (no clock, no sensor).
- Lights (Connect, Art-Net / sACN): when the app goes to the background with the song stopped,
  when a light output is switched off or pointed at another receiver, and when a universe is no
  longer used, every universe it lit gets a dark frame (heads keep their position). Blackout now
  also darkens the one fixture without a rig. Coming back, the light fades up at the flash limit.
- Chase MTC: with Loop on, the song follows the sender instead of being thrown back to bar 1;
  the loop rests while the sender runs. A MIDI loop take keeps its passes when the chase starts.
- The Echoel Synth plug-in: a value set from the plug-in's view during a host's automation ramp
  is no longer overwritten by the ramp.
- Arrangement: "Duplicate as Linked" and "Make Unique" for clips.
- "Transcribe…" on an audio part or video part: subtitles from speech recognized on the device
  (languages whose model is installed), export as SRT, WebVTT or OTIO markers.
- A song saved by a newer build opens; parts this build does not know are kept inactive.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10051) — ADM BWF export, Learn, MIDI Time Code. Earlier: git history.
group.com.echoelmusic is in the app's entitlements since a14e1960a (F17, 2026-10-21); the import
of earlier songs has not been seen on a device yet.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. Clicks: play a song with an audio track from the middle of a region, jump, pause and play;
   in AUM or GarageBand, automate the Echoel Synth's cutoff and turn the knob during the ramp.
   No click anywhere, and the knob keeps the value you turned to?
2. Chase MTC from QLab or Reaper with Loop on, sender running past the song's end. Does the song
   follow the sender (not bar 1) and stop within a moment when the sender stops?
3. A track's Modulate, Pan, "Bar LFO → Pan", play. Does the pan swing once per bar, and does an
   exported WAV swing the same way?
4. Art-Net to a node or a DMX monitor, no fixtures patched, light on: Blackout on; then play,
   stop, go to the home screen. Does the light go dark both times, and fade up when you return?
5. "Transcribe…" on a spoken take in a language your phone has installed. Do subtitle cues
   appear on the timeline, and does the SRT export open in a video player?
